How far away the game still draws things. Beyond the draw distance, the world fades out - a balance between looking real and running well on a small phone.A non-player character: a person in the game world who is run by the game, not by a human. NPCs walk, drive, work, and can talk with you.Words that re-wrap to fit any screen or font size, instead of being frozen onto a fixed page the way a PDF freezes them.The place and moment where the player (or a character) appears in the world. In Surviving Adamsville you spawn at 535 Dollar Mill Road - home.The shape of the ground itself: hills, dips, creek beds, and banks. In the redraw, the terrain is built from real elevation measurements.A marked point the game uses to guide movement - a bus stop, a street corner, a destination. The GPS arrow leads you from waypoint to waypoint.One named region of the game world. Adamsville is a single zone; the whole map is divided into zones so the game only has to draw the one you are standing in.